{%- comment -%}
  SEO metadata backfill.

  Horizon's stock snippets/meta-tags.liquid only emits a meta description when the
  page's SEO description is filled in in the Shopify admin, and only emits an
  og:image when Liquid can resolve a `page_image` — which never happens on custom
  /pages/* templates. The practical result was that every marketing page on this
  site shipped with no meta description and no social share image.

  This snippet fills both gaps WITHOUT duplicating tags: each block is guarded so it
  only fires when the stock snippet did not already emit that tag. Anything set in
  the Shopify admin always wins.

  Rendered from layout/theme.liquid immediately after 'meta-tags'.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- capture fallback_desc -%}{%- render 'kw-seo-desc' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign fallback_desc = fallback_desc | strip -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Keep the leftover storefront out of the index. Kilowash sells an installed service,
  but Horizon still serves product, collection, cart and search pages, and Shopify
  lists an empty blog and its privacy-choices page in the sitemap. None of them can
  rank for anything a homeowner searches, and every one Google indexes is a thin page
  diluting the ten that matter. "follow" keeps any links on them counted.

  The blog drops out of the noindex on its own the moment it has a published post.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign kw_noindex = false
  case request.page_type
    when 'product', 'collection', 'list-collections', 'search', 'cart'
      assign kw_noindex = true
    when 'blog'
      if blog.articles_count == 0
        assign kw_noindex = true
      endif
    when 'page'
      if page.handle == 'data-sharing-opt-out'
        assign kw_noindex = true
      endif
      comment
        A city page with no body of its own is the same page as every other city with
        the name swapped: a doorway page. It stays out of the index until someone
        writes its local copy (see sections/kw-city-intro).
      endcomment
      if template.suffix == 'city' and page.content == blank
        assign kw_noindex = true
      endif
  endcase
-%}
{%- if kw_noindex -%}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}Only fires when the admin SEO description is empty — no duplicates.{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if page_description == blank and fallback_desc != blank -%}
  <meta name="description" content="{{ fallback_desc | escape }}">
{%- endif -%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Same rule as meta-tags: a page's own image (product, article, collection) wins;
    everywhere else the Kilowash share image beats the store-wide Preferences image.
  endcomment
  assign share_image = null
  assign own_image = false
  if page_image
    if request.page_type == 'product' or request.page_type == 'article' or request.page_type == 'collection'
      assign own_image = true
    endif
  endif
  if own_image
    assign share_image = page_image
  elsif settings.kw_seo_share_image != blank
    assign share_image = settings.kw_seo_share_image
  elsif page_image
    assign share_image = page_image
  elsif settings.logo != blank
    assign share_image = settings.logo
  endif
-%}

{%- if share_image -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    og:image is emitted here exactly when meta-tags did not emit the stock one.
    twitter:image is always emitted — meta-tags.liquid never emits one at all, so
    link previews on X/Slack/iMessage currently fall back to nothing.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- unless own_image or settings.kw_seo_share_image == blank and page_image -%}
    {%- comment -%}Cropped to 1200x630, the ratio Facebook, iMessage and X all render without trimming.{%- endcomment -%}
    <meta property="og:image" content="{{ share_image | image_url: width: 1200, height: 630, crop: 'center' | prepend: 'https:' }}">
    <meta property="og:image:secure_url" content="{{ share_image | image_url: width: 1200, height: 630, crop: 'center' | prepend: 'https:' }}">
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
  {%- endunless -%}
  <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ share_image | image_url: width: 1200, height: 630, crop: 'center' | prepend: 'https:' }}">
{%- endif -%}
